Twenty-first pass: additional libraries and authorization outcomes
=================================================================

20 contracts: 15 USDT in four libraries and three base tools/daemons, and five
kernel contracts in MAC ABAC and OpenEndpointSecurity. Four installed profiles.
Existing ABAC allow/deny and OES allow/deny/timeout probes are retained. New
probes add reasons and scalar values missing from those contracts. No command,
label text, path, credential, secret, capability token or message ID is added.

New kernel contracts (provider sdt, empty module/function)
--------------------------------------------------------
abac-check-bypass(op, missing_subject, missing_object): existing null-label
allow shortcut, before return; not a newly introduced authorization exemption.
abac-rule-decision(rule_id, set, operation_mask, result): matched rule, with
result=0 or EACCES; set comes from the rule iteration under the read lock.
abac-default-decision(operation_mask, default_policy, result): no matching
rule. default_policy=0 allows, other values deny under existing semantics.
oes-auth-flags(event_type, result, allowed_mask, denied_mask): accepted first
flag response while the pending event is locked. Masks describe the response,
not necessarily the final combined authorization of every listening client.
oes-response-rejected(error, has_flags, proposed_result): invalid flag-based
response for an event type (EINVAL), already responded/expired (EALREADY), or
unknown/non-auth message (ESRCH). No dereference after release. Existing auth
allow/deny/timeout and wait probes cover ordinary outcomes and deadline policy.
All five use inline SDT patchpoints guarded by !cold; no early boot, interrupt
entry, DTrace internals, extra clocks or allocations are instrumented.

New userland contracts
----------------------
oesclient (liboes):
 batch-read(bytes,error): raw batch read outcome, including short reads (EIO).
 buffer-corrupt(buffered_bytes,offset): malformed buffer before its reset.
 auth-response(proposed_result,allowed_mask,denied_mask,error): one event per
 response attempt, including invalid client, invalid flags response result,
 short write, write failure and accepted write. Plain responses use zero masks.
 A successful write is submission success, not proof the operation is allowed.
timecmp (libtimecmp):
 wait-start(client_identity), wait-done(client_identity,error,malformed): wait
 for FIDL completion, including transport errors, deadline expiry and application
 status. No extra clock query. The wrapper disappears when tracing is disabled.
 reply-malformed(error): invalid result shape/value or protocol version.
capsuleclaims (libcapsulert):
 rights-parsed(kind,result,mask): jail=1, file=2, storage=3. Success exposes the
 parsed rights mask; error exposes zero, even if parsing partially filled output.
 No textual manifest is collected. Disabled builds retain the original body.
shmring (libshmring):
 record-reject(error,required_or_observed_bytes,available_bytes): short record
 header, impossible record length or insufficient destination buffer. Existing
 successful read/write probes remain the success path. Ring indices are not
 reread for tracing, and payloads are never copied into probes.
abacdaemon (mac_abacd), abacctl (mac_abac_ctl):
 policy-start(command), policy-done(command,error): management mac_syscall
 results before logging, cleanup or errx. Covers good and bad kernel results;
 does not expose the opaque command argument or configuration text.
oeslogger:
 event-handled(event_type,message_size): validated event delivered to handler;
 the site is before handler invocation, so it does not guarantee output success.
 wait-done(poll_result,error): polling including timeout/interruption/failure.
 dispatch-error(stage,error): batch read=1, dead/error poll descriptor=2.
 The standalone example remains usable without base's FIVEBSD_TRACE definition.

Validation and limits
---------------------
14 native library/tool builds with MK_DTRACE=yes/no. DOF inspection checks real
probe sites and arity, and absence from disabled builds. MAC ABAC and OES modules
link; four kernel on/off source builds pass -Werror. Linked modules contain six
new executable sites for the five contracts (response rejection has two sites).
No modules were loaded. These checks do not claim live authorization probes
fired; /dev/dtrace is unavailable on the running host.
Existing liboes tests use pipes and mock allocation/ioctl paths to verify owned
versus borrowed descriptors, invalid descriptors, allocation failure and path
bounds. Claim-parser tests run against both new library variants. No policy is
loaded, power/time operation issued, or production daemon started.

